From e14cda3c39dd96e7193352748759e856579f0747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:46:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] bitproxy: every sing-box server type, safer reloads,
 battery-friendly checks

Servers:
- Import share links (vless, vmess, trojan, ss, hysteria2/hy2, hysteria,
  tuic, anytls, socks, http(s), naive, ssh), subscriptions (base64 or
  plain, by URL), sing-box JSON (outbounds/endpoints or a whole config)
  and OpenVPN .ovpn profiles (openvpn-client endpoint; username and
  password are added in the app).
- Non-WireGuard servers are stored as sing-box JSON, join the VPN group
  with any TUN address, and resolve VPN-app DNS over TCP 1.1.1.1.
  Selecting one uses the default TUN 172.19.0.1/30.
- The diagnostics export also removes passwords, UUIDs and OpenVPN keys.

Reliability:
- Every reload (Apply, app installed/removed, IPv6) has a 20 s watchdog
  and a traffic check 5 and 20 s later; a dead tunnel restarts the
  process cleanly (at most every 10 min). Android doesn't restart a
  killed VPN service, so a 30 min start alarm acts as a dead man's switch.
- Health checks: every 3 min with the screen on, every 15 min with it
  off, never in Doze, and right away when the screen turns on. Only for
  WireGuard groups (not every proxy type carries UDP).
- App installs and removals are written to the events log.

UI: paste links/URL, server rows show the type, the Servers and Apps
cards on the Dashboard start collapsed.
